WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.419 --> 00:00:01.989
(light playful music)

00:00:01.989 --> 00:00:04.043
- [Narrator] This is the Spider tortoise.

00:00:04.043 --> 00:00:06.957
These little guys are so
endangered that scientists say

00:00:06.957 --> 00:00:11.124
that they could completely
vanish in the next 15 years.

00:00:12.989 --> 00:00:15.624
The Spider tortoise is hard to find.

00:00:15.624 --> 00:00:17.560
For one, they're tiny.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.049
One of the smallest known land-turtles,

00:00:20.049 --> 00:00:23.578
rarely reaching more than
six inches in length.

00:00:23.578 --> 00:00:26.397
Another reason, they only
inhabit a tiny sliver

00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:29.571
of Madagascar's southwestern coast.

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:33.260
Their name comes from the
web-like patterns on their shells.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.224
During the dry season, they
bury themselves in the sand,

00:00:36.224 --> 00:00:37.634
and reemerge when it rains

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:40.939
to feed on leaves, roots, and insects.

00:00:40.939 --> 00:00:43.668
Just because they're tiny
doesn't mean they're young.

00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:47.410
They're estimated to live
up to 70 years in the wild.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.886
These little guys are up against a lot.

00:00:49.886 --> 00:00:52.507
The largest concern is that
they are still hunted locally

00:00:52.507 --> 00:00:55.949
for food, but the illegal pet
trade, and shrinking habitat,

00:00:55.949 --> 00:00:58.240
are all threats to their survival.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.805
This is the Spider tortoise.

00:01:00.805 --> 00:01:03.972
(light playful music)

